Slab Scanner n2: tiles only, three readers, the distance by the codes' size; what the first two native files said

Tests 1 and 2 with n1 (9 and 14 inches): 47 and 48 right codes of 50, none wrong, 45 and 42 of them within half a
second (the web app: half by 2.4 s). The file showed that Apple's reader finds nothing in the whole 12 MP picture - it
reduces whatever region it is given - while tiles find every code, the finer the tile the better for the fine codes;
that the depth sensor's (smoothed) distance was wrong at these distances (2 m for 213 mm); and that frames from before
the record tap were read into the test.

n2: four, nine, sixteen and thirty-six tiles in turn, three frames at a time; no read under confidence 0.5 counts; the
distance by the size of the codes (a slab's barcode is 17.5 or 18.4 mm wide) on the screen and in the report; the
depth sensor unsmoothed, with its quality flags; frames from before the tap left out. CLAUDE.md: the numbers.

